   {
    "id": "L0.2",
    "title": "Letter Forms: One Letter, Four Shapes",
    "level": 0,
    "minutes": 20,
    "explain": [
     "Every letter changes shape depending on WHERE it sits in a word: isolated (alone), initial (start), medial (middle), final (end).",
     "Most letters have TWO tails: a connecting tail (like ـبـ) used inside words, and their own shape at word ends.",
     "Six letters are 'proud' — they refuse to connect to what comes AFTER them: ا د ذ ر ز و. They only connect on their RIGHT side."
    ],
    "interactive": {
     "kind": "forms"
    },
    "drills": [
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "Which letter NEVER connects to the following letter?",
      "options": [
       "ب",
       "م",
       "د",
       "س"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "The initial form of م is:",
      "options": [
       "مـ",
       "ـمـ",
       "ـم",
       "م"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "In the word كتاب (kitab), the ب appears in which form?",
      "options": [
       "isolated",
       "initial",
       "medial",
       "final"
      ],
      "answer": 3,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "How many non-connecting letters are there?",
      "options": [
       "4",
       "5",
       "6",
       "7"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "match",
      "pairs": [
