 "1": {
  "title": "Reading",
  "subtitle": "Harakat to fluency",
  "lessons": [
   {
    "id": "L1.1",
    "title": "Short Vowels: Fatha, Damma, Kasra",
    "level": 1,
    "minutes": 20,
    "explain": [
     "Arabic short vowels are small MARKS above or below letters (harakaat):",
     "• Fatha َ (above): 'a' sound — بَ = ba\n• Damma ُ (above, tiny waw): 'u' sound — بُ = bu\n• Kasra ِ (below): 'i' sound — بِ = bi",
     "Unvoweled text (like newspapers) omits these — but the Quran ALWAYS shows them. That's why we learn with mushaf-style text."
    ],
    "interactive": {
     "kind": "vowels"
    },
    "drills": [
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "بَ reads as:",
      "options": [
       "bi",
       "bu",
       "ba",
       "ab"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "The kasra ِ gives which sound?",
      "options": [
       "a",
       "u",
       "i",
       "e"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "Where is the damma written?",
      "options": [
       "below the letter",
       "above the letter",
       "after the letter",
       "before the letter"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "مُ reads as:",
      "options": [
       "mu",
       "mi",
       "ma",
       "um"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "match",
      "pairs": [
       [
        "بِ",
        "bi"
       ],
       [
        "بُ",
        "bu"
       ],
       [
        "بَ",
        "ba"
       ]
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "L1.2",
    "title": "Sukoon: The Silent Mark",
    "level": 1,
    "minutes": 15,
    "explain": [
     "Sukoon ْ sits ABOVE a letter and means 'no vowel here' — the letter closes the syllable.",
     "بَبْ = bab (two beats: ba-b). Every syllable is either open (CV: بَ) or closed (CVC: بَبْ).",
     "This is the rhythm engine of Arabic reading."
    ],
    "drills": [
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "أَبْ reads as:",
      "options": [
       "aab",
       "ab",
       "abi",
       "ba"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "Sukoon means the letter has…",
      "options": [
       "a long vowel",
       "no vowel",
       "double sound",
       "an echo"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "كَتَبْ has how many syllables?",
      "options": [
       "1",
       "2",
       "3",
       "4"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "match",
      "pairs": [
       [
        "بْ",
        "no vowel"
       ],
       [
        "بَ",
        "short a"
       ],
       [
        "بُ",
        "short u"
       ]
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "L1.3",
    "title": "Tanween: The Indefinite '-n'",
    "level": 1,
    "minutes": 15,
    "explain": [
     "Tanween doubles the vowel mark and adds an 'n':",
     "• Fathatan ً : بً = ban\n• Dammatan ٌ : بٌ = bun\n• Kasratan ٍ : بٍ = bin",
     "Tanween marks INDEFINITE nouns (a house vs THE house). It's the grammar of 'a/an'."
    ],
    "drills": [
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "كِتَابٌ reads as:",
      "options": [
       "kitaban",
       "kitabun",
       "kitabin",
       "kitab"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "Fathatan ً adds which ending?",
      "options": [
       "-un",
       "-in",
       "-an",
       "-een"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "بَيْتٍ ends with:",
      "options": [
       "-an",
       "-un",
       "-in",
       "silent"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "match",
      "pairs": [
       [
        "بً",
        "ban"
       ],
       [
        "بٌ",
        "bun"
       ],
       [
        "بٍ",
        "bin"
       ]
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "L1.4",
    "title": "Long Vowels: Madd",
    "level": 1,
    "minutes": 15,
    "explain": [
     "Stretch each short vowel with its long partner:\n• ا after fatha: بَا = baa (2 beats)\n• و after damma: بُو = buu\n• ي after kasra: بِي = bii",
     "Rule of thumb: long vowel = hold 2 counts. In the Quran some stretches run 4–6 counts (tajweed madd) — we'll mark those later."
    ],
    "drills": [
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "قَالَ reads as:",
      "options": [
       "qala",
       "qaala",
       "qila",
       "qul"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "بِي stretches the sound:",
      "options": [
       "a",
       "u",
       "i",
       "none"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "mc",
      "q": "A natural madd lasts about:",
      "options": [
       "half beat",
       "1 beat",
       "2 beats",
       "6 beats"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "hint": ""
     },
     {
      "type": "match",
      "pairs": [
       [
        "بَا",
        "baa"
       ],
       [
        "بُو",
        "buu"
       ],
       [
        "بِي",
        "bii"
       ]
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "L1.5",
    "title": "Shadda: The Doubler",
    "level": 1,
    "minutes": 15,
    "explain": [
     "Shadda ّ fuses two identical letters into one written shape: read it twice.",
     "مُحَمَّد = mu-ham-mad (the م is doubled). First half carries the previous vowel, second half gets its own.",
     "Pattern: Cَ + Cْ merged = Cَّ ."
